{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/399054-so-2nd-edition-sold-me-on-requiem-what-to-do","id":399054,"title":"So, 2nd Edition sold me on Requiem, what to do...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-09T11:17:59-08:00","id":399054,"title":"So, 2nd Edition sold me on Requiem, what to do...","content":"As it was suggested to me some time ago by the ever helpful Rose Bailey, I finally got around to reading the 2nd ed core, and the book did for me what the 1st edition core didn't, and made me like VtR, and more importantly, it made me want to run it (and play it, but more and more I discover I prefer STing/GMing rather than playing).<br /> <br /> What I'm asking is what books, if any, from the 1st edition run I should check out (I already know about Damnation City). I'm also wondering if the 1st ed Demo could played with 2nd edition rules, mostly because Reaping Whirlwind seems to be for a more experience party of players and characters.<br /> <br /> Also, how married is the game to the mechanics of Doors, and Mask and Dirge? The first is my least liked portion of the new ruleset and one I will almost certainly throw out, and the second seems too much like Nature/Demeanor, which I always disliked, much preferring the Virtue/Vice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T12:14:33-08:00","id":399163,"title":"","content":"All three can easily be thrown out without ever even thinking about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T12:24:39-08:00","id":399174,"title":"","content":"I agree, most things can be shifted or changed. I am not a giant fan of the doors either, so I rarely use them when STing. However I find that the mask/dirge allows you to be more unique at character creation than vice/virtue concept allowed. You wont end up with several players with the same combo. It also gives clearer parameters on how to get back willpower, just food for thought ^.^ you could easily play with Vice/Virtue instead.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T13:01:47-08:00","id":399204,"title":"","content":"Thanks. My dislike of Mask and Dirge is due to the fact that Nature and Demeanor rarely, if ever, came up during our games, while in our changeling one-shot Virtues and Vices were pretty heavily featured, and felt important to the characters.<br /> <br /> Nothing on the Vampire Demo stories? Can they played with no changed beyond the different mechanincs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T13:14:35-08:00","id":399216,"title":"","content":"Well for one they won't have Predator's Taint, so that changes a teeny tiny bit.<br /> <br /> Otherwise yeah, you could run pretty much any SAS for Vampire with little to no changes involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T13:31:40-08:00","id":399225,"title":"","content":"You can run Danse de la Mort (the first demo) with 2e rules.<br /> <br /> This forumite did a pretty thorough conversion and then did a short actual play of their experiences. I think Danse de la Mort does a good job of introducing new players into the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/44219-danse-de-la-mort\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/44219-danse-de-la-mort\"> Danse de la Mort - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/44219-danse-de-la-mort\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/44219-danse-de-la-mort </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Given that our three-years ongoing VtR game will be rocking characters with 90+ Experiences when we fully convert over to the B&amp;S rules update, I'm toying with the idea of continuing on with the Danse de le Mort demo chronicle I had started a while back, updated for the new system. This should give us a less </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:04:34-08:00","id":399292,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot, that was exactly what I needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:34:32-08:00","id":399363,"title":"","content":"Unless you are truly set on using Virtues and Vices (as said, it takes no effort to change that part) may I suggest using the Masquerade and Requiem from Danse Macabre instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T15:05:27-08:00","id":399396,"title":"","content":"Well, I believe I've said I've never had interest in Requiem before now, so I have no idea what's in what book, or what those are. So, what do Masquerade and Requiem do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T15:27:17-08:00","id":399414,"title":"","content":"Masquerade is a &quot;vampire role archetype&quot;, basically what do you do as a kindred, your niche inside the danse macabre. Your Masquerade is what you pretend to be to the mortal world, what ruse you use to move around without arising suspicion. There are ten samples of each in the book, though is not necesarily a closed list (but is a good starting point and the archetypes are broad enough to fit most character concepts).<br /> <br /> They have some mechanical backing in the form of specific 1-5 tiered Merits (similar to Styles) but can be used instead of Virtue (Masquerade) and Vice (Requiem). Mask and Dirge were originally to be like that and somehow ended up similar to Nature and Demeanor.<br /> <br /> If the problem is that they wouldn't be relevant, I think Masquerade and Requiem are pretty defining of the kind of character you want to play, and some pairings may even spark some character concepts if you are short on ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-09-2015, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T15:32:37-08:00","id":399417,"title":"","content":"Thanks you, that does sound interesting. I'll check those out once I can get the book you mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T16:03:04-08:00","id":399493,"title":"","content":"Though I believe it's mentioned in a B&amp;S sidebar, Blood Sorcery: Sacrements and Blasphemies sounds useful if you or one of your players wants to use the Lance or the Crone, or if you want to introduce a bloodline or Covenant with its own Blood Sorcery, especially since those rules are the basis for the current ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T00:26:43-08:00","id":400100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/399054-so-2nd-edition-sold-me-on-requiem-what-to-do?p=399363#post399363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you are truly set on using Virtues and Vices (as said, it takes no effort to change that part) may I suggest using the Masquerade and Requiem from Danse Macabre instead?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But... but... Those <b><i>are </i></b>the mask/dirge and they work in pretty much the same way. One being his role as Kindred, and the other being what he's pretending to the kine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T02:25:41-08:00","id":400125,"title":"","content":"Not at all the same, no. For starters there's a different list for Masquerades and Requiems and what represents is similar, yet different. Mask and Dirge are more (way more!) like Nature and Demeanor than Requiem and Masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T05:01:13-08:00","id":400179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/399054-so-2nd-edition-sold-me-on-requiem-what-to-do?p=400125#post400125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not at all the same, no. For starters there's a different list for Masquerades and Requiems and what represents is similar, yet different. Mask and Dirge are more (way more!) like Nature and Demeanor than Requiem and Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree with Griautis on this one. Not having read the Masquerade/Requiem part of Danse Macabre, you described what the Mask and Dirge are, and named them Masquerade/Requiem.<br /> <br /> As I see it (and I'm speaking about what they represent, not the mechanics behind them):<br /> <br /> \u00b7 Nature/Demeanor spoke about the inner self of the character: how he/she was and how he/she projected him/herself to the outside world.\u00b7<br /> <br /> \u00b7 Mask/Dirge (and Masquerade/Requiem for what you're describing) are more related to the position/context of the character in the Mortal/Kindred world than about their inner psychology. If there's any similarity to Nature/Demeanor, both of these would be Demeanor, the first towards the mortals, the second towards the vampires.<br /> <br /> Also, the fact that the list of &quot;archetypes&quot; for Masquerade/Requiem and Mask/Dirge is different doesn't really matter, as it is always implied that they are examples and you can come up with new ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3719,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3719-cable","user":"Cable","date":". 02-10-2015, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3719-cable","name":"Cable","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3719_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T05:41:33-08:00","id":400188,"title":"","content":"In response to what first edition books to take a look at:<br /> <br /> Clanbooks, clanbooks, clanbooks. The clanbooks are well written, evocative, present plot hooks without resolving or firmly defining them, have some cool bonus material like the Hollow Mekhet, and are an important element of Requiem defining itself as a thing in its own right rather than a successor to Masquerade, in the way that the 2e VtR corebook carries onward. If you've ever wondered how Requiem Ventrue are supposed to be any different from Masquerade Ventrue besides a tacked-on clan weakness sop to Malkavians, well. These are the books that will answer questions like that. (I actually like the 1e Ventrue weakness, I'm just describing one possible impression it could make.)<br /> <br /> Beyond that it's a question of what interests you and what you like about the game. Some of my picks: The Danse Macabre for a bunch of mechanical hacks and additional covenants, although DM was so influential on the second edition rules that half of its ideas are kind of covered already. Ancient Mysteries for flashpoints of moments in Kindred history and the strange things they carried, or Ancient Bloodlines for the player options complement to those strange things. Night Horrors: Wicked Dead for the weird things that resemble the Kindred but are not Kindred, such as the alien forebears and cousins of clan Jiang-shi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T05:47:08-08:00","id":400196,"title":"","content":"I use the lists interchangeably between the two... the lists are pretty similar, while the ones in Danse Macabre are more expanded since they have more word count devoted to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T07:26:10-08:00","id":400295,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with Griautis and Cable. Mask/dirge are almost the same thing as Requiem/Masquerade, it even says they are archetypes. A Good roleplayer will already be using some of these things, you just get mechanics to go with them. you might make a character that is a drug addict.... then just pick junkie for your Dirge. It is bound to come up in the game. Or if your concept for the character is to be a strong leader, pick authoritarian for the mask. You might be using them and not even know it &gt;.&gt; - Take the Drug addict one, it's way easier to take Junkie than it is to deal with Lust/Gluttony, but that's my opinion. They are just suggestions too. I had to make up a few too that werent on the list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T12:38:19-08:00","id":426841,"title":"","content":"I have to ask, since I hadn't somehow noticed, but does it change much having 5 players instead of 4? One of each clan, instead of the separated Nosferatu/Edward like in the scenario?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T20:39:47-08:00","id":427325,"title":"","content":"There are mechanical differences between mask/dirge and masquerade/requiem. One was based on the other so thematically they are the same when you remove the mechanics. I don't like to quote large sections of book text, but since it might help you out to see how the new was before. Here is Nomad from Dance Macabre.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Nomad is bound to no domain, and owes no Prince obedience. She\u2019s got freedom, for what that\u2019s worth, but also no protection or authority or safe place to crawl back to when the world gets cruel. There\u2019s something unsettled about the Nomad that makes staying put an exercise in willpower.<br /> <br /> It used to be damned near impossible for a true nomad to wander between domains, back before the interstate highway system, air freight, ocean liners, and the telecommunications. Now all an anarchic misanthrope needs is a car and a roll of tinfoil and duct tape for covering up the motel room windows. At 65MPH, you can cover 600 miles of road easy. Get a room on the other end, or park the car somewhere safe and sleep in the trunk. When it was travel by horse or on foot, only the Gangrel could do it safe, sleeping in the Earth\u2019s Embrace. Now any itchy-foot neonate can hit the open road and cruise into a domain ahead of the sun. <br /> <br /> But, who\u2019s going to welcome them?<br /> <br /> A domain is a carefully balanced social ecology, and outsiders have a way of fucking such careful balances up pretty bad. The young Nomad will soon realize how unwelcome she is in most places. Princes take a dim view of unaligned unattached Kindred rolling into their towns without knowing the score, and the power players tend to start licking their lips thinking about the new tasty morsel. The flipside of the modern ease of travel is the speed that news travels- as soon as somebody spots you squeezing the local fruit, their texting your description to their allies, and moving in to see if you\u2019re a resource they can exploit (or worse for you, one their enemies can exploit), a threat to their plans, or just somebody to keep a close eye on. <br /> <br /> Surviving as a Nomad requires patience and diplomacy, and it requires the ability to quickly create working rapports with the local big kids. Arriving at a new city you\u2019ve never been to before is nerve-racking, but a place where you know some people, and where some people know you is much more hospitable. Presenting yourself to the Prince ASAP is always a good plan unless the domain has gone feral. If it\u2019s a democratic anarchy, then it\u2019s trickier because you have to figure out who the big players are before making yourself know. But once you\u2019re let the local boss know who you are, and that you\u2019re not going to make any trouble, they\u2019ll usually give you only the minimum amount of grief. They might ask you to take some letters or a package to an associate in another domain, and the more letters of introduction you can collect by playing nice with the politicos the easier time you\u2019ll have. <br /> <br /> Some princes employ Nomads as messengers, using their impulse to wander to their advantage. A prince\u2019s messenger is usually a pretty tough individual, as there\u2019s many who\u2019d like to get their mitts on a Prince\u2019s private correspondences.&quot;<br /> <br /> Obviously, that is much more depth that a 2-3 sentence blurb. I can understand how the brevity might bring up memories of Nature/Demeanor. They are similar ideas, but this Requiem description still works for the equivalent Dirge. This is not a valid description of a Nature, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T20:53:49-08:00","id":427345,"title":"","content":"Mask/Dirge is the mechanism for Vampires to regain Willpower so if you switch them out for Virtue/Vice then you need to be careful about making sure they are used enough to get adequate Willpower to players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}